<article class="env-definition" id="FCDB5F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/FCDB5F">Definition <span data-tag="FCDB5F">5.3.1.1</span>.</a>filtered!topological category Let $\calC $ be a topological category. We will say that $\calC $ is <em>filtered</em> if it satisfies the following conditions: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1')$"><p>
For every finite set $\{ X_ i\} $ of objects of $\calC $, there exists an object $X \in \calC $ and morphisms $\phi _ i: X_ i \rightarrow X$. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2')$"><p>
For every pair $X, Y \in \calC $ of objects of $\calC $, every nonnegative integer $n \geq 0$, and every continuous map $S^ n \rightarrow \bHom _{\calC }(X,Y)$, there exists a morphism $Y \rightarrow Z$ such that the induced map $S^ n \rightarrow \bHom _{\calC }(X,Z)$ is nullhomotopic. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>